{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790284750,"nonce":"DRTY3c36cgqhuBPlQzhQJqnrEBY=","title":"Lua typer: a field or element only ever stored from its own read stays untyped and reads as nil","message":"A store whose value depends on a read of the same slot never gets a type: the read of a field (or element, or dynamic slot) nothing typed has been stored in yields Unknown (\"decides nothing yet\"), so the value stored is Unknown, the slot stays Unknown, and at the end of inference Unknown settles to Nil. The lowering then reads the slot as nil every time.\n\n    local o = {}\n    for i = 1, 3 do o.n = (o.n or 0) + 1 end\n    print(o.n)\n\nlua5.4 prints 3, zylua prints 1 (main 678f49eb). The same happens to an array part whose only store is `c[w] = (c[w] or 0) + 1`, depending on what else is in the chunk (a counting loop over ipairs printed 1 1 1 instead of 1 1 3 once a float table and a closure preceded it). Counting into a table under string keys hits it as soon as those reads are typed.\n\nFix: once the rounds converge, set a settling flag and run rounds again in which a read of a slot nothing typed was stored in yields nil (nothing stored), so the store is typed from it; converge again.","files":null}]}